--TEST--
`Core\Cli\Text::plain` is idempotent, so text that has already passed a sink is not escaped twice — ADR 0086 §§ 1-2
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 1's table is idempotent: a Control Picture is not a control byte, so a
// second pass changes nothing. That is what lets `Core\Out::capture`'s already
// neutralized bytes and `plain`'s answer be the same kind of value without
// either of them double-escaping the other — the second escape `rule:security/capture-answers-the-carrier`
// exists to prevent.
var $raw = Core\Str::fromCodePoint(27) . "]0;title" . Core\Str::fromCodePoint(7);
echo Core\Cli\Text::plain($raw), "\n";
echo Core\Cli\Text::plain(Core\Cli::escape($raw)), "\n";
echo Core\Cli\Text::plain(Core\Cli::escape(Core\Cli::escape($raw))), "\n";
--EXPECT--
␛]0;title␇
␛]0;title␇
␛]0;title␇
